| explorer | hit | HEAD `4cafeea`: task selection by comma list at `benchmark/run.py:979-983,1040` and repo filter at `run.py:1095-1100`; `--modes` and `--experiment` already form a mutually exclusive group at `run.py:984-993`; `TASKS` lookups inside cells at `run.py:479,518`; per-row metadata merge at `run.py:1193-1202,1232`; local repo setup at `run.py:1113-1137`; registry at `benchmark/tasks/__init__.py:80-147`; repo languages at `benchmark/config.py:101,110-140`; manifest-validation pattern at `benchmark/variants.py:45-113`; results JSONL are gitignored (`.gitignore:37`), so the lock reads the c1 store, not result files; c1 landed at `87f2e73`: path-taking store functions at `benchmark/baselines.py:78-80,83,97,102`, store path at `benchmark/run.py:1436`, per-cell metadata and store calls at `run.py:1519,1532-1542,1573,1591,1606`, analysis accuracy at `benchmark/analyze.py:59,180-214` |

## Approach

1. **Fixtures first.** Commit fixture panels under `benchmark/tests/fixtures/panels/`: one complete panel with three FeatureBench ids and the two SWE-bench Multilingual primaries, one complete panel using both fallbacks, and the malformed variants the tests parametrize. Commit c3's own fixture dataset rows and tiny bare repositories for the Go slot, the Rust slot, and one FeatureBench instance. Tests stub only `admit`, the store path, and the model-runner launch (F-1).
2. **Store read.** Add `baselines.rows(path, *, panel_name=None)` to `benchmark/baselines.py` as a read-only iterator over stored rows (G-1, G-2, G-3).
3. **Loader.** A new `benchmark/panels.py` `load_panel(path, *, store_path, admit)` parses the file, checks schema, family, language, fallback, and tier rules, resolves local members from `TASKS` and external members through `external.featurebench.load` and `external.swebench_ml.load`, checks languages against `REPOS` and the dataset rows, computes `stratify` and `split_digest`, refuses missing required members, calls `admit` for each external member, and checks the split lock against `baselines.rows(store_path, panel_name=name)`. It returns `Panel(name, cheap, dev, test, split_digest, members)` or raises `PanelError` (G-1, G-2, G-3, F-1).
4. **Run wiring.** `run.py` gains `--panel` and `--panel-split`. Inside `main`, after argument checks and before the MCP preflight, it calls `load_panel` with `RESULTS_DIR / baselines.STORE_FILENAME`, registers the external tasks into `TASKS`, and sets `tasks_list` to the selected members. The cell loop adds `Panel.stamp(task_name)` to the per-cell metadata, so it reaches each row before `baselines.store`. External members run through c2 hooks with no container (F-1).
5. **c5 hand-off.** c3 fixes the `run.run_plan(cells, *, panel, ledger, candidate_sha, refreeze_baselines)` signature and its stamp test; c5 implements it, stamping before `baselines.store` on the same path. c5 `evolve.main` loads the panel only through `load_panel` with the same store path.
6. **Analysis.** `analyze.load_results` counts a contaminated panel row as incorrect, keeps it in the denominator, and the report adds a per-task and per-arm contaminated tally (G-1, G-3, F-1).
7. **Commit the panel.** Run c2 preflight on the cook host, list the admitted FeatureBench Lite Level 1 instances, fill fallbacks only for primaries whose preflight fails (recording the reason), write `benchmark/panels/gepa-v1.json` through `panels.stratify`, capture each external member's dataset row from the pinned revision into `benchmark/tests/fixtures/panels/gepa-v1-rows/`, and commit both before any paid run (G-1, G-2, G-3, F-1).

## Interface sketches

```text
slice:            benchmark (existing harness) + new benchmark/panels.py and benchmark/panels/
spine step:       workflow (run.py task selection and cell loop)
public interface: panels.load_panel(path, *, store_path, admit=external.preflight.admit) -> Panel(name, cheap, dev, test, split_digest, members); raises PanelError on any schema, language, completeness, admission, or split-lock fault; the only way any caller (run.py, c5 evolve) obtains a Panel  (G-1, G-2, G-3, F-1)
public interface: Panel.stamp(task_name) -> {panel_name, panel_split_digest, panel_split}, merged before baselines.store  (G-1, G-2, G-3)
public interface: panels.stratify(members, split_seed) -> dict[id, dev or test]  (G-2, G-3)
public interface: baselines.rows(path, *, panel_name: str | None = None) -> Iterator[Row]; read only; path explicit like load_rows, lookup, and store; c3-added seam on c1 module, c1 contract unchanged  (G-1, G-2, G-3)
public interface: run.run_plan(cells, *, panel: Panel, ledger, candidate_sha, refreeze_baselines) -> list[Row]; required panel; stamps before baselines.store; signature defined by c3, implemented by c5  (G-1, G-2, G-3)
public interface: analyze.load_results counts a row with panel_name and contaminated true as incorrect, kept in the denominator, with a per-task and per-arm contaminated tally  (G-1, G-3, F-1)
store path:       RESULTS_DIR / baselines.STORE_FILENAME, passed by run.py and c5; tests pass a temp path
public interface: run.py --panel PATH --panel-split {cheap,dev,test,all}  (F-1)
consumed:         external.preflight.admit(instance_id) -> PreflightVerdict; external.featurebench.load / external.swebench_ml.load -> ExternalTask with its dataset row language  (c2, F-1)
consumed:         c1 is_completed, load_rows, store  (c1); c2 contaminated row field  (c2, F-1)
private:          panel JSON schema, fallback pair table, digest canonicalization, completeness and split-lock helpers
crust delta:      new row fields panel_name, panel_split_digest, panel_split (not run-key inputs); new run.py flags --panel and --panel-split; new benchmark/panels.py; new baselines.rows; run.run_plan panel parameter; analyze contaminated tally; new benchmark/panels/gepa-v1.json and its fixture rows
arrows:           run.py -> panels -> tasks, external (preflight, loaders); panels -> baselines (row read); no container runtime anywhere on the path  (F-1)
```

## Acceptance
- AC-1: WHEN `run.py --panel PATH` is given a panel holding every required member with every external member admitted THE SYSTEM SHALL load it into `Panel(cheap, dev, test)` with the three local hard tasks in `cheap` and the stratified assignment in `dev` and `test`, resolve local members from `TASKS` and FeatureBench and SWE-bench Multilingual members through `external.featurebench.load` and `external.swebench_ml.load`, invoke the runner once per selected member, model, mode, and repetition for the `--panel-split` selection, and start no `docker`, `podman`, or other container process.  (G-1, G-2, G-3, F-1)
- AC-2: WHEN any caller, including `run.py --panel` and a direct non-run.py caller such as c5 `evolve.main`, calls `panels.load_panel` on a panel that lacks any one required member (at least one FeatureBench Lite Level 1 task, `gin_edit_render_context`, `rg_search_dispatch`, `rg_trait_implementors`, `gin_servehttp_flow`, the Go SWE-bench Multilingual slot, or the Rust SWE-bench Multilingual slot), or WHEN `external.preflight.admit` returns a non-admitted verdict for any external member, THE SYSTEM SHALL raise `PanelError` naming each missing or unadmitted member, and `run.py --panel` SHALL exit nonzero before any runner call.  (G-1, G-2, G-3, F-1)
- AC-3: WHEN a SWE-bench Multilingual slot is filled by its fallback THE SYSTEM SHALL accept it only when it carries `fallback_for` naming that slot's primary and a non-empty `fallback_reason`, include the fallback id in the split digest, and refuse a slot holding both its primary and fallback, a fallback paired with the other slot's primary, or a fallback without `fallback_for` or `fallback_reason`.  (G-3, F-1)
- AC-4: WHEN a panel loads THE SYSTEM SHALL keep exactly `rg_search_dispatch`, `rg_trait_implementors`, and `gin_servehttp_flow` in the cheap tier and out of `dev` and `test`, assign the other members by family-stratified alternation over `(language, sha256("<split_seed>:<id>"))`, and refuse a file whose recorded split differs from that assignment or that marks any other member `cheap`.  (G-2, G-3)
- AC-5: WHEN a panel run through `run.py --panel` or `run.run_plan` produces a row THE SYSTEM SHALL stamp `panel_name`, `panel_split_digest`, and `panel_split`, outside the run key, before `baselines.store`, and on the output copy of a reused row; WHEN `baselines.rows(path, panel_name=name)` is called THE SYSTEM SHALL yield exactly the stored rows stamped with that name without writing the store; WHEN any caller of `panels.load_panel` finds a completed stored row with the same `panel_name` and a different `panel_split_digest` THE SYSTEM SHALL raise `PanelError`, and `run.py --panel` SHALL exit nonzero before any runner call; WHEN every completed stored row for that panel name carries the current digest, or none exists, or only error, quota, or timeout rows carry a different digest, THE SYSTEM SHALL load the panel.  (G-1, G-2, G-3)
- AC-6: WHEN a panel file has an unknown key, a duplicate id, an unknown local task, a member outside the required families and ids (including an unknown `family` value and a `swebench_ml` id outside the Go and Rust slot table), a local member whose language differs from its repo language, a `featurebench` member whose language is not `python`, a Go or Rust slot member whose language is not `go` or `rust` respectively or differs from its dataset row `language`, or an external task name that collides with a `TASKS` entry, or WHEN `--panel` is combined with a non-default `--tasks` or `--repos`, THE SYSTEM SHALL exit nonzero before any runner call and name the fault.  (G-2, G-3, F-1)
- AC-7: WHEN the committed `benchmark/panels/gepa-v1.json` is loaded with its committed fixture dataset rows, through the real c2 row-to-`ExternalTask` path and with no network or host `$TILTH_BENCH_DATA`, THE SYSTEM SHALL return a panel holding at least one FeatureBench Lite Level 1 member, `gin_edit_render_context`, the three local hard tasks in the cheap tier, one Go and one Rust SWE-bench Multilingual slot member, every declared language equal to its dataset row `language`, and a recorded split equal to `panels.stratify` for its seed.  (G-1, G-2, G-3)
- AC-8: WHEN `analyze.py` reports rows carrying `panel_name` THE SYSTEM SHALL count every row with `contaminated: true` as incorrect, keep it in its task and arm denominators, and report a per-task and per-arm contaminated tally; WHEN rows carry no `panel_name` THE SYSTEM SHALL report them as before.  (G-1, G-3, F-1)

