## Non-goals
- Admission mechanics, native checkouts, environment builds, grading, and contamination scanning (child `bench-external-tasks`, c2).
- Applicability labels and their slicing (c4) and how the evolution loop consumes tiers and splits, beyond the `run.run_plan` panel parameter c3 defines (c5).
- Producing the `contaminated` flag (c2); c3 only consumes it in analysis.
- A panel unlock or relock flag; a changed split is a new panel name.
- Containers of any kind (F-1).
- Changes to `src/**`, `prompts/**`, or any tilth binary behavior.
- Bumping the crate or npm version (fork law).

